# This figure contains FontImage material glyphs: icons at three positions, which is why the differing columns come in three runs.
#
# Java2D rasterizes the same glyph from the same bundled font at the same size
# slightly differently on macOS and Linux. Measured against the CI runner's own
# output: 368 differing pixels of 129244, 0.2847% of the image, worst channel
# delta 136. The differing pixels fall in narrow column runs the width of an
# icon, at the icon positions; every text column is byte-identical, so this is
# edge coverage on the glyphs and nothing else. Layout is untouched -- both
# renders are exactly the same size.
#
# The committed image is the CI runner's output, so the gate that actually runs
# compares byte-for-byte and this budget is what lets a developer regenerate the
# figure on a Mac. Both bounds bind independently. maxMismatchPercent limits how
# much of the image may change AT ALL -- every differing pixel counts, not only
# those past the delta -- so a wholesale recolour cannot creep through in small
# steps. maxChannelDelta then caps how far one pixel may move; 160 clears the
# measured worst with room while a solid overwrite still fails it.
maxChannelDelta=160
maxMismatchPercent=0.4
